|~ `::null`, the kind of the absent value, its constructor, and the
   soft read of it. ~|

::null
  |~~ The kind of null, the absence of a value; a slot a call may leave
      empty declares `::null` among its kinds. A kind of the core is
      named under its prefix and written short, `::qlang/null` reading as
      `::null`, and its constructor reads a payload of the kind as the
      value itself. ::link~(::verb | doc)
      ::link~(::qlang | doc :values)

      ~(null | type | eq ::null)
      ~(::qlang/null | eq ::null)
      ~(::null(null) | eq null)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/type/null}

::NullPayloadNotNullError
  |~~ `::null` reads its payload as null; a payload of another kind is
      refused.
      ~(
        ::null(1)
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::NullPayloadNotNullError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

:at
  |~~ Null, whatever the place: a soft read of the absent value is
      absent, so soft reads chain, `at :address | at :city`, and a
      `coalesce` after them gives the fallback once. The strict `/k`
      refuses null as it refuses every value without parts.

      ~(null | at :k | eq null)
      ~({:a null} | at :a | at :b | coalesce "none" | eq "none")
      ~({:a {:b 1}} | at :a | at :b | eq 1)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:place ::any | :returns ::null | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/at})
